bration or held-out split before scoring.\n3. Enumerate the intervention registry R from the public WAM implementation. Each r=(branch, module, denoising_step, axis) identifies one actual quantization hook in the coupled video/action denoiser, with axis in {weight, activation}; exclude VAE-only, text-only, latent/action tokenizer, and planner-only sites. Output a deterministic registry with a lexicographic tie-break order and a mapping from each site to its real kernel and exact bit setting. Reject an empty registry before ranking.\n4. Measure single-site model interventions with matched stochastic state. For every r and calibration item j, restore an independent clone of S_j before each branch, including controller state, simulator RNG, model RNG/generator, observation/history buffers, and persistent model cache; then run F_0 and F_r with the same h_j, l_j, xi_j, and inference path. Record the full action chunks a_j0 and a_jr and the hook outputs y_jr0 and y_jrr. Define the open-loop local surrogate L_jr as the mean squared difference over all elements of y_jr0 and y_jrr, and L_r as the episode mean of L_jr. Use fake-quant/dequantized GEMM only as a profiling implementation; record whether it was used and keep it separate from the real low-bit-kernel evaluation. Output paired model traces indexed by (j,r).\n5. Execute paired environment counterfactuals. Restore independent clones of S_j, including z_j, controller state, simulator RNG eta_j, observation/history buffers, model RNG/generator state, and persistent cache, for the two traces. Apply the first executable action after the restored controller's identical action transformation to each full chunk, and record o_(j+1)0, o_(j+1)r, and the simulator's independent contact/task-transition state. The downstream output of this step is the actual next observation and state transition caused by the altered first action, not merely a changed intermediate discrepancy; C_r therefore does not estimate effects of executing later chunk actions or subsequent replanning.\n6. Compute the consequence object. Define sigma_a^2 as the population variance over all scalar coordinates of all FP16 full action chunks in D_cal, and sigma_o as the mean of the population per-pixel standard deviations of FP16 next observations across D_cal. Use named floors epsilon_a=epsilon_o=1e-3 in normalized units, with a pre-registered 1e-4/1e-3/1e-2 sensitivity check. Compute d_a and d_o as the normalized full-action-chunk MSE and next-observation per-pixel L1 differences, set lambda_a=lambda_o=1 by default with a held-out sensitivity sweep over lambda_a/lambda_o in {0.5,1,2}, and output C_r as their episode mean with bootstrap intervals over complete episodes. C_r is a one-control-transition action/observation proxy, not task-success loss.\n7. Replace the local allocation operator without retraining. Define B_site, with B equivalent to B_site everywhere in this method, as the nonnegative integer high-precision-site count recorded by the matched local-fidelity baseline in the pre-registered run manifest; halt if that entry is missing or B_site>|R|. Rank sites by C_r and upgrade exactly the top-B_site sites while leaving all other sites at b_lo; resolve ties by the registry order. This primary comparison is a site-count budget only, not a claim of equal bytes or latency. For every schedule, record a separate deployment-cost ledger covering persistent weight bytes including copies and scales, peak live activation workspace under the real kernel, and measured latency; do not substitute that ledger for B_site or call the quantities equivalent.\n8. Run the confound-isolating diagnostic. On the same episodes, compare L_r and C_r using Spearman rank correlation separately on simulator-identified contact/task-transition and non-contact subsets, then compare top-B_site C_r allocation against top-B_site L_r allocation and a score-permuted negative control. If fewer than two sites exist, or either score vector is constant in a subset, record Spearman as undefined and skip that correlation rather than fabricate a value. The reported object is the divergence in downstream action/observation and task metrics, not a claim that a correlation itself is causal.\n9. Validate the selected schedule on held-out RoboTwin 2.0 and LIBERO episodes with the real low-bit kernel. Compare FP16, the matched local-fidelity baseline, the C_r allocation, and uniform precision at the same B_site site-count budget; measure task success, contact-sensitive failure rate, full action-chunk deviation, next-observation deviation, peak memory, and latency, with the same Fast-WAM configuration and multiple episode seeds.\n10. Keep CPU arithmetic checks and deployment claims separate. CPU runs may verify site indexing, deterministic paired seeds, scale normalization, and C_r arithmetic only; they do not establish robot success, GPU memory, or speedup. Report any LingBot-VA replication as a separate calibration/inference experiment with its offload and checkpoint configuration, and do not combine fake-quant traces with real-kernel performance.",
